```

''Standing of the field citations:'' the research spirit marked four of its highest-value
sources as fetched-at-403 — search digests, never the papers. Every number below carries the
confidence its spirit vowed, and the digest-only ones cap near 12/20. Open the papers before
quoting any of them onward.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-gate>>

!! The Gate

The myth already wrote the arithmetic, and the instrument MUST NOT improve on it:

<<< 
Is there something nearby worth surfacing, and will the cost of interrupting be less than
the cost of silence? When the answer is yes, it speaks — briefly, with high signal, and then
returns to watching.
<<<

The field supplies the threshold the myth left as a feeling.

Google's Tricorder ships a check only under ''< 10% effective false
positives'', where an ''effective false positive'' names a finding ''the operator took no
action on''. A finding that reads correct and gets ignored has failed identically to one that
reads wrong.

The definition relocates truth: ''the operator sets the false-positive rate, never the check
author''. A check the operator keeps waving past does not stand vindicated by being right.

!!! The discredited channel

Drug-interaction alerts run ~10% clinical relevance and reach ''90%
physician override'' — and ''88.2% of very-severe alerts get overridden too''. Once a channel
discredits itself the severity field carries no force.

''Law:'' severity inflation spends a reserve that never refills. The instrument MUST NOT
raise an item's rank to win attention it did not earn.

!!! Habituation arrives on exposure two

fMRI work measured visual-processing collapse ''after the second
exposure''; polymorphic presentation resisted it where fixed presentation did not.

''Law:'' the instrument MUST NOT render the same item identically on repeat. An item either
changes shape or stops surfacing.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/tiers>>

!! The Ladder as Budget

The myth scales KAIROS by node tier — Household a faint one-line flag, Crossroads detectable,
Temple full assessments unprompted. That ladder carries a noise governor, and the alarm
standards give it an envelope.

EEMUA 191 / ANSI-ISA-18.2 name ''>10 items in 10 minutes'' as an
''alarm flood'' — the point a human stops processing items one at a time.

| Tier | Myth signal | Proposed cap |
|---|---|---|
| Household | "a faint note at the end of a session, a one-sentence anomaly flag" | 1 |
| Crossroads | KAIROS detectable | 3 |
| Temple | "full assessments unprompted" | 5 |

''The numbers came from this design pass, never from the myth'' — which names no integers
anywhere. ''Ruled adopted (operator, 2026-08-27); this lararium stands at Temple, cap 5.''
A node surfacing ten items has left the ladder rather than climbed it.

!!! Overflow — the cap governs SURFACING, never finding

A wide sweep finds more than a tier surfaces, and the two MUST NOT be reconciled by widening
the cap. Renovate's dependency dashboard names the pattern: ''a small surfaced set, plus one
standing place where the remainder stays inspectable on demand''.

# The sweep runs wide and ranks everything it finds.
# The tier surfaces its cap — 5 here — and no more.
# The remainder rests at one addressable place the operator MAY open by asking; it MUST NOT
push, and the surfaced set MUST name how many wait behind it.
# A finding held back by overflow MUST NOT count as dismissed — it never reached the operator,
so it spends neither compliance nor reliance (#trust-ledger).

!!! Never silent

A randomized field experiment (n=237) measured notifications ''off
entirely'' scoring ''worse'' than the status quo — more anxiety, not less; coarse batching
(3×/day) won, while hourly batching bought nothing over control.

The house already holds this as law — `focus="N/<band>"` rides every turn, and the signal room rules
''Aperture — never silent''. The instrument MUST report ''checked, nothing stands'' rather
than fall quiet. Silence reads as absence, and absence reads as broken.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/anatomy>>

!! Check Anatomy

The contract already stands at `integration-check.ts` as `{ name, ok, detail }` — cheap,
running on every stand. KAIROS extends the same shape rather than raising a second one.

| Field | Carries | Grounds |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | a `lar:` URI naming the ''drift class'', never the instance | the addressing law gives stable finding identity for free; `git fsck` message-IDs name the same need |
| `stands` | held · clear · ''inconclusive'' | Scorecard's `-1`; the house reads it as avaktavya — the pole where the true/false axis does not fit |
| `detail` | what the check saw, in one line | the existing contract |
| `dimensions` | the evidence carried beside the verdict | Powerpipe: a finding ships with its own grounds |
| `fix` | the one-line corrective the operator MAY run | Google's gate — an item with no action attached MUST NOT ship |
| `receptivity` | whether the operator can act ''now'' | see #two-gates |
| `stage` | the 0–20 band the item surfaces at | the house's own ladder |

!!! Two gates, not one

The JITAI literature names two conditions — ''vulnerability'' (the
need exists) and ''receptivity'' (the person can act) — and its own systematic reviews record
that receptivity ''almost never gets measured''. The field named the right variable and then
failed to instrument it.

''Drift alone MUST NOT fire.'' A dirty tree, a rebase in flight, a live incident all read as
low receptivity: a true finding stays withheld, kept for the next coarse breakpoint.

!!! The moment

Session boot stands as a ''coarse breakpoint by construction'' — no
task in flight, so no resumption lag to pay. The wake hook already fires there. Mid-session
surfacing MUST clear a much higher bar.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/refusal>>

!! The Refusal to Act

The instrument surfaces; the operator acts. The wake hook already rules this for its own
reason, and KAIROS inherits it rather than arguing it:

<<< 
`--observe` withholds the standing half: the frame still reports the node, the recall and the
sidecar, while standing one remains the operator's act.
<<<

`brew doctor` holds the same discipline — it prints, exits nonzero,
and leaves the corrective command to the operator. Google's contrary rule (fix automatically
what can be fixed automatically) holds ''only under code review'', where a human approves the
diff before it lands. An unattended scheduled runner carries no equivalent consent gate, so
the rule MUST NOT port without it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/decay>>

!! Decay — the re-entry key

The field research returned this gap open and refused to fill it: no literature found on
which findings expire and which persist.

''The house already holds the model.'' A finding the operator sets down files a `kue` —
attributed dissent carrying a ''re-entry key'': the named condition under which the dispute
reopens. A dismissed check neither expires on a timer nor persists forever; ''it sleeps until
its key turns''.

A study across 1,425 projects found suppressions mostly
''undocumented'', encoding technical debt and tool misassumptions that never reached the check
author. The `kue` form cannot go undocumented — it requires the reason and the key.

''Laws:''

# A dismissal MUST bind to the `lar:` id — the drift class, never the instance.
# A dismissed finding MUST NOT resurface unchanged. A finding returning after dismissal
teaches the operator that dismissal does nothing, and that lesson generalizes to every check.
# A dismissal MUST route to the ''check'', never only to the instance. Google's "Not useful"
button files against the ''analyzer author'', and analyzers with high dismissal rates ''get
disabled''. A dismissal that silences one instance teaches the instrument nothing.

<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/hoike">>

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/trust-ledger>>

!! The Trust Ledger — two accounts, never one

Dixon & Wickens separate two channels that MUST NOT trade against
each other:

<<~ scale compliance "acting-when-it-fires ~ degraded by FALSE ALARMS">>
<<~ scale reliance "trusting-the-silence ~ degraded by MISSES">>

''A quiet run makes a claim.'' Suppressing a noisy check to protect compliance draws down
reliance, and nothing surfaces that draw unless the instrument counts both.

Two counterweights against over-tuning: reliability as low as 0.6
still aided performance, and the cry-wolf effect measured weaker than assumed in air traffic
control. Perfect precision does not name the bar.

Parasuraman & Riley name the failure this guards: ''disuse'' — neglect of ''reliable''
automation, root-caused to false alarms and to a base rate nobody weighed.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/check-set-one>>

!! Check Set One

Drawn from the sweep that occasioned this room. Each carries a `lar:` id, a cheap test, and a
one-line fix.

| `lar:` id | Holds when | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `lar:///allow-rule.path.dissolves` | a rule names a path that no longer resolves | drop the rule |
| `lar:///allow-rule.wildcard.overreaches` | a `*` sits before the rest of the command | move the `*` past the verb, or drop |
| `lar:///allow-rule.interpreter.opens` | a rule matches the vendor's stripped-interpreter class | drop; a pattern cannot bound an interpreter |
| `lar:///deny-list.stands.empty` | `permissions.deny` carries nothing | seat a floor the allow side cannot lift |
| `lar:///sandbox.stands.unconfigured` | the OS boundary sits off while the allow-list carries one it cannot hold | configure filesystem + network together |
| `lar:///mcp-record.names.the-departed` | enabled/disabled MCP entries name servers no config defines | clear the stale names |
| `lar:///vessel.sock.stands.absent` | a configured MCP holder exits for want of the daemon | `lares vessel stand` |

!!! The law under the first three

''A pattern can bound the string; only a runtime can bound the
authority.'' Wherever an allowed program can name another program — `-c`, `-e`, `-exec`,
`--pre`, `--compress-program`, `core.fsmonitor` — the allow-list has delegated its whole
authority to a string the pattern never sees.

Three independent lines converge: the vendor strips the class in auto mode rather than
publishing a safe glob for it; sudoers reached the same place decades earlier, and its
`NOEXEC` interposition leaks through `system()`/`popen()` by its own advisory; and the eight
published Claude Code escapes land at the ''argument'' layer, never the verb.

''You can allow-list an interpreter invocation. You cannot allow-list an interpreter.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ruled>>

!! Rulings — operator, 2026-08-27

| Fork | Ruling |
|---|---|
| Tier cap | 1/3/5 adopted; ''this lararium stands at Temple'' — 5 items surfaced at boot |
| Seat | ''its own verb'' — `lares kairos` stands alone; the wake hook calls it ''beside'' `vessel stand --observe`, so boot carries both frames |
| Scope | ''wider posture sweep'' — permissions, sandbox and deny floor, repo and config drift, MCP topology, hook paths |
| Exec-shaped allow-rules | ''cut'' — five wildcarded interpreter grants plus the stdin-fed `Bash(python -)` that carried no wildcard for any glob check to catch |

!!! The tension the rulings carry

Widest sweep, tightest surfacing. The two hold together only through #tiers overflow, and the
instrument MUST NOT resolve them by widening the cap when the ranking gets hard. A sweep that
finds forty things and surfaces five stands healthy; one that surfaces forty has become the
alarm flood the standard names.

!!! Standing open

# ''Cadence'' — session boot alone, or boot plus a coarse scheduled sweep. Boot stands as the
free coarse breakpoint; a scheduled sweep needs its own justification.
# ''Ledger persistence'' — where compliance and reliance counts live across sessions.

<<~/ahu>>

